# Feature branch required

Do not implement or commit work on `master`.

- Before the first edit, run `git status --short` and `git branch --show-current`.
- Continue on the current branch only when it already belongs to the requested work.
- Otherwise create a `feat/…`, `fix/…`, or `chore/…` branch from current `master`.
- If the worktree is dirty, stop and ask before switching or creating a branch. Do not stash, discard, or carry unrelated changes.
- Review the branch and staged diff before committing. Do not merge or push to `master` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Deliver new work through a pull request.

```powershell
git status --short
git switch -c feat/session-cleanup master
```
